+`parseRanges(text, pageCount)` reads what a person typed into the page box
+and returns the page numbers to print as an array. Pages are numbered from 1
+to `pageCount`. The text consists of comma-separated parts, where each part is
+either a single page number or a range written as `first-last`. A `text` that
+is not a string throws a `TypeError`; a `pageCount` that is not a positive
+integer throws a `TypeError`; a text that cannot be read as pages of this
+document (e.g., a page past the last one, a page 0, or a non-numeric part)
+throws a `RangeError`.
